\f0\fs24 \cf2 And here we are in the Gallery of Arms, one of the most dramatic rooms in the entire house. It feels like stepping into a chivalric novel: armors silently observing, swords hanging as if still ready for use, and a layout that is, incredibly, almost identical to what the Bagatti Valsecchi brothers envisioned. The only missing element? The banners that once adorned the walls like a grand noble curtain. But even without them, the atmosphere remains powerful: each object is a small time machine, ready to transport us into the Renaissance dream of those who imagined and lived in this house.}